ever falling back to Markdown, so a fixture-completeness gap surfaces as a red test instead of a vacuous pass.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.3767,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Current fixture stores exactly 884 pass-1 entries keyed by input_sha256 (generate_dc_wiki_legacy_outputs.py: _EXPECTED_UNIT_COUNT = 884; entries keyed by 'input_sha256').","test_dc_corpus_passes_two_to_five_are_byte_identical feeds each body's pass-1 OUTPUT back through render_markdown_to_wiki, generating pass-2 prepared units whose SHA-256 keys differ from the 884 pass-1 keys (test_wiki_render_corpus.py lines 282-289).","The existing live converter legacy_convert returns None on any failure (generate_dc_wiki_legacy_outputs.py lines 185-189) and render_markdown_to_wiki degrades to original Markdown on None — a static converter that mirrors this on a key miss would hide the miss."],"finding":"The plan's static-converter mechanism does not specify lookup-miss behavior, so an input the production renderer produces during settling/dispatch that is absent from the committed fixture could silently fall back to Markdown and make the richness, settling, and byte-output assertions pass vacuously.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f08baf9e2e30c813b","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan section 'Plan', bullet 2 ('Add a test-only static converter backed by those committed artifacts. Drive the production segmenting renderer through that converter ...')","norm_id":"n1aded867db52dd54","priority":0.2233,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A settling pass produces a prepared unit whose hash is not in the fixture; the static converter returns None; the renderer emits the input verbatim; test_dc_corpus_passes_two_to_five_are_byte_identical still 'settles' and passes while covering nothing."],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.3333,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context"